<p>
  {dgettext("help_channels", "Limits the maximum number of users that can be in the channel.")}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "When to use it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Use a user limit to keep a room small. It helps when a channel is meant for a team, a class or a game group. It also slows down a crowd that arrives all at once."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_terminal}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Usage")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/mode +l 25  {dgettext("help_channels", "Set limit to 25 users")}
/mode -l     {dgettext("help_channels", "Remove user limit")}</pre>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "The command changes the channel you are looking at. You do not type the channel name."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_general}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Central")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Operators can also open Channel Central, go to the Modes tab, tick Limit, type the number and choose Apply Modes."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Rules and limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Only channel operators and owners can set or remove the limit.")}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "The limit must be a whole number greater than zero. If the number is not valid, the limit does not change."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "When the channel has as many members as the limit, the next person who tries to join is refused with a message that the channel is full."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Lowering the limit never removes anyone. People already inside stay in the channel."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "An invitation does not get around the limit. Bots in the channel count as members."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "In a registered channel the limit is saved and comes back after a restart."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_channels", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-mode">{dgettext("help_channels", "/mode")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="mode-j">{dgettext("help_channels", "Join Throttle (+j)")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-modes-overview">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Modes Overview")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
